  "facts": [
    "Konak Tunnel, a 1,674‑meter twin‑bores road tunnel, opened on 25 May 2015, easing traffic in İzmir’s Konak district by cutting through 100 meters of earth beneath the city.",
    "Construction began on 23 September 2011 and cost ₺150 million, with Prime Minister Ahmet Davutoğlu officially inaugurating the tunnel during his visit to İzmir.",
    "The tunnel forms part of a 7‑kilometer express route, linking central Konak with the İzmir Coach Terminal in Bornova alongside the Buca‑Bornova Tunnel."
